ttps://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Significant-Hobbies/reader/commit/421a3c476a6b9c69afd92fdad7a01463b5a8dc42","node_id":"C_kwDOQfeY39oAKDQyMWEzYzQ3NmE2YjljNjlhZmQ5MmZkYWQ3YTAxNDYzYjVhOGRjNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Significant-Hobbies/reader/commit/de3a01b0414d95f3fd4c901066bc87ce221979e3","sha":"de3a01b0414d95f3fd4c901066bc87ce221979e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Significant-Hobbies/reader/commits/de3a01b0414d95f3fd4c901066bc87ce221979e3"}],"sha":"421a3c476a6b9c69afd92fdad7a01463b5a8dc42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Significant-Hobbies/reader/commits/421a3c476a6b9c69afd92fdad7a01463b5a8dc42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/43884471?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sarthakagrawal927","id":43884471,"login":"sarthakagrawal927","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzODg0NDcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sarthakagrawal927","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Significant-Hobbies/reader/commits/de3a01b0414d95f3fd4c901066bc87ce221979e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:23:39Z","email":"43884471+sarthakagrawal927@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Sarthak Agrawal"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-23T06:23:39Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(app): add the Microsoft Clarity tag to the app shell (#53)\n\nAdds Microsoft Clarity (session replay + heatmaps) to app.html, the entry\npoint for the authenticated SPA served at /app.\n\nNot merged as-is on purpose — see the PR. Two things need a decision first:\n\n1. src/pages/PrivacyPage.tsx says \"No third-party tracking pixels or\n   marketing tags.\" Clarity is a third-party tag, so that line stops being\n   true the moment this ships.\n\n2. app.html is the app shell, not a landing page. Session replay there can\n   record what the reader is actually reading — saved article and PDF\n   content, annotations, board contents, and chat questions — which is the\n   private material the product exists to keep private (\"Research library:\n   capture, annotate, and AI-chat over your reading — private by default\").\n   Whether Clarity''s content masking is set to strict for this project\n   determines whether that happens, and that is a setting in the Clarity\n   dashboard, not in this repo. I cannot verify it from here.\n\nVerified locally (Node 24.19.0):\n\n  pnpm format:check  Checked 168 files in 37ms. No fixes applied.\n  pnpm lint          Lint: 0 errors, 38 warnings across 194 files.\n                     (unchanged from main — app.html is excluded from Biome\n                     by \"!**/*.html\")\n  pnpm typecheck     tsconfig.app.json + tsconfig.worker.json — clean\n  pnpm test          Test Files 18 passed (18), Tests 97 passed (97)\n  pnpm build         ✓ built in 474ms\n\n  the tag reaches the built shell:\n    dist/app.html  1 occurrence of clarity.ms/tag/y6budslpbi\n\nThe Clarity project id is a public client-side site key, not a secret.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9d33263fdca8ceda13cb2a8dd0ad8b2d13259353","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Significant-Hobbies/reader/git/trees/9d33263fdca8ceda13cb2a8dd0ad8b2d13259353"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Significant-Hobbies/reader/git/commits/de3a01b0414d95f3fd4c901066bc87ce221979e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 9d33263fdca8ceda13cb2a8dd0ad8b2d13259353\nparent e8e1043c731dc783eaa6668fe772d71d8bf17f19\nauthor Sarthak Agrawal <43884471+sarthakagrawal927@users.noreply.github.com> 1787466219 +0530\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787466219 +0530\n\nfeat(app): add the Microsoft Clarity tag to the app shell (#53)\n\nAdds Microsoft Clarity (session replay + heatmaps) to app.html, the entry\npoint for the authenticated SPA served at /app.\n\nNot merged as-is on purpose — see the PR. Two things need a decision first:\n\n1. src/pages/PrivacyPage.tsx says \"No third-party tracking pixels or\n   marketing tags.\" Clarity is a third-party tag, so that line stops being\n   true the moment this ships.\n\n2. app.html is the app shell, not a landing page. Session replay there can\n   record what the reader is actually reading — saved article and PDF\n   content, annotations, board contents, and chat questions — which is the\n   private material the product exists to keep private (\"Research library:\n   capture, annotate, and AI-chat over your reading — private by default\").\n   Whether Clarity''s content masking is set to strict for this project\n   determines whether that happens, and that is a setting in the Clarity\n   dashboard, not in this repo. I cannot verify it from here.\n\nVerified locally (Node 24.19.0):\n\n  pnpm format:check  Checked 168 files in 37ms. No fixes applied.\n  pnpm lint          Lint: 0 errors, 38 warnings across 194 files.\n                     (unchanged from main — app.html is excluded from Biome\n                     by \"!**/*.html\")\n  pnpm typecheck     