eived_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/commits/3485fd2a0eb408e4a8b770ab0b88141b3d37b813/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-31T08:50:23Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-31T08:50:23Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"message":"fix(auth): address PR review comments for firebaseAuthService\n\nAddresses CodeRabbit and GitHub Copilot PR review feedback:\n\n1. Remove hardcoded Google client ID fallback - Now requires\n   GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID env var and throws clear error if missing\n2. Add configuration state tracking to prevent retry spam on failure\n3. Wrap fallback callback(null) in try-catch to prevent exceptions\n   from bubbling up and breaking the Firebase listener\n4. Improve error messages with context about which callback failed\n\nChanges:\n- Added googleSignInConfigurationAttempted and googleSignInAvailable flags\n- Validate GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID presence and fail fast if not set\n- Prevent repeated configuration attempts after first failure\n- Enhanced error handling in onAuthStateChanged with nested try-catch\n  for both primary callback and fallback callback(null)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"16417fcc97644926657f41f06223698929c31143","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/git/trees/16417fcc97644926657f41f06223698929c31143"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/git/commits/3485fd2a0eb408e4a8b770ab0b88141b3d37b813","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau","id":810357,"login":"pateatlau","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDM1Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/commit/3485fd2a0eb408e4a8b770ab0b88141b3d37b813","node_id":"C_kwDOQfmMHtoAKDM0ODVmZDJhMGViNDA4ZTRhOGI3NzBhYjBiODgxNDFiM2QzN2I4MTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/commit/49e465a929a4da2c2454442679194552d3c4124c","sha":"49e465a929a4da2c2454442679194552d3c4124c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/commits/49e465a929a4da2c2454442679194552d3c4124c"}],"sha":"3485fd2a0eb408e4a8b770ab0b88141b3d37b813","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/commits/3485fd2a0eb408e4a8b770ab0b88141b3d37b813"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/810357?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pateatlau","id":810357,"login":"pateatlau","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDM1Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pateatlau","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/commits/49e465a929a4da2c2454442679194552d3c4124c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-01-31T08:35:24Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-01-31T08:35:24Z","email":"pateatlau@gmail.com","name":"Patea Tlau"},"message":"fix(auth): resolve Android release build login screen loading issue\n\nFixes the indefinite loading spinner on Android release builds by:\n\n1. Deferred Google Sign-In configuration to avoid calling native modules\n   at module load time, which can fail in Hermes release builds\n2. Added robust error handling to onAuthStateChanged with fallback callback\n3. Implemented 10-second failsafe timeout set BEFORE any async operations\n4. Ensured isInitialized is always set to true, even on errors\n\nThe root cause was that Firebase auth initialization could fail silently\non Android release builds, and the auth store would never set isInitialized\nto true, causing the login page to show a spinner forever.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"918de2691e6f5076f5287b3945dad7ec1e977a12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/git/trees/918de2691e6f5076f5287b3945dad7ec1e977a12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pateatlau/universal-mfe-2026/git/commits/49e465a929a4da2c2454442679194552d3c4124c","verification"