c3a84","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/77f545195f74cada2bc2ad5f1ad11c4e175c3a84"}],"sha":"f8ec477783988ac56a8ca999bb7aa4e6685e3deb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/f8ec477783988ac56a8ca999bb7aa4e6685e3deb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20647751?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon","id":20647751,"login":"catastrophe-brandon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQ3NzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/77f545195f74cada2bc2ad5f1ad11c4e175c3a84/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-13T22:59:06Z","email":"btweed@redhat.com","name":"Brandon Tweed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-13T22:59:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"More fumbling in the dark with dev proxy routes (#13)\n\n* More fumbling in the dark\n\n* lint\n\n* Updated docs\n\n* fix: correct Caddy environment variable syntax in proxy template\n\n## Problem\nThe proxy ConfigMap template was using incorrect Caddy syntax for\nenvironment variable substitution: {env.HCC_ENV_URL}\n\nThis caused Chrome shell routes to fail because Caddy couldn''t resolve\nthe stage environment URL.\n\n## Solution\n- Changed template to use correct Caddy syntax: ${HCC_ENV_URL}\n- Updated all test expectations to use correct syntax\n- Added validation checks in 7 tests to prevent regression\n\n## Changes\n- template/proxy_caddy.template.j2: Fixed env var syntax\n- tests/*: Updated assertions and added negative validation\n- CLAUDE.md: Added comprehensive documentation about:\n  - Correct vs incorrect Caddy syntax\n  - New \"Common Issue\" entry for this problem\n  - CRITICAL warnings to prevent future regressions\n\n## Test Coverage\nAll proxy generation tests now verify that {env.HCC_ENV_URL} does NOT\nappear in generated configs, ensuring the correct ${HCC_ENV_URL} syntax\nis always used.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: use direct URL substitution and remove routing directives from app ConfigMap\n\n## Changes\n\n### Direct URL Substitution\n- Added --stage-env-url CLI argument (required when Chrome routes exist)\n- Template now uses direct substitution: {{ stage_env_url }} instead of ${HCC_ENV_URL}\n- Eliminates Caddy environment variable resolution issues\n- Validation fails with clear error if stage_env_url not provided\n\n### Removed Routing Directives from App ConfigMap\n- Removed all try_files and rewrite directives from app template\n- App container only serves static files (fed-mods.json, JS bundles)\n- Proxy handles all routing logic\n- App ConfigMap now only contains asset routes (/apps/*, /settings/*)\n\n### Updated Validation\n- Renamed validate_federated_module_config → validate_app_config\n- Now validates NO app configs contain try_files or rewrite\n- Added tests for both try_files and rewrite rejection\n\n### Test Coverage\n- Updated all 29 tests to provide stage_env_url values\n- Added validation tests to prevent routing directives in app configs\n- Tests verify no ${HCC_ENV_URL} or {env.HCC_ENV_URL} in generated files\n\n## Breaking Change\n--stage-env-url is now REQUIRED when generating proxy ConfigMaps with Chrome routes\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove leading/trailing whitespace from generated ConfigMaps\n\n## Problem\nGenerated ConfigMaps had extra blank lines at the start of the data\nsection, causing yamllint to fail when committing the files.\n\n## Solution\n- Added .strip() to clean template output before indenting\n- Fixed Jinja2 template to use {%- and -%} for whitespace control\n- Removed leading/trailing newlines from rendered content\n\n## Result\nGenerated ConfigMaps now pass yamllint validation without extra\nblank lines at the start of data sections.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove catch-all root handler from app ConfigMap\n\n## Problem\nThe app ConfigMap template had a catch-all `handle /` directive that would\nredirect to /apps/chrome/index.html. This was problematic because:\n\n1. The app container on port 8000 should never receive requests to /\n2. The proxy routes /* to the stage environment, not localhost:8000\n3. This catch-all could interfere with routing if proxy logic changes\n4. It''s unnecessary - app container only serves its asset routes\n\n## Solution\nRemoved the `handle /` block entirely from app_caddy.template.j2\n\n## Result\nApp ConfigMap now only contains handlers for its specific asset routes:\n- /apps/rbac\n- /settings/rbac\n\nNo catch-all routes that could interfere with proxy routing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update CLAUDE.md to reflect proxy architecture changes\n\nUpdate documentation to reflect the new architecture where app ConfigMap\nonly serves static assets and proxy ConfigMap handles all routing logic.\nDocument direct URL substitution approach via --stage-env-url argument.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a34265c0edbb0e4241ecbef0753eb8bb24523cdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/trees/a34265c0edbb0e4241ecbef0753eb8bb24523cdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/commits/77f545195f74cada2bc2ad5f1ad11c4e175c3a84","verification":{"payload":"tree a34265c0edbb0e4241ecbef0753eb8bb24523cdb\nparent d245396e6fc456987d7c0d0c1360d46b1e499894\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1771023546 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1771023546 -0600\n\nMore fumbling in the dark with dev proxy routes (#13)\n\n* More fumbling in the dark\n\n* lint\n\n* Updated docs\n\n* fix: correct Caddy environment variable syntax in proxy template\n\n## Problem\nThe proxy ConfigMap template was using incorrect Caddy syntax for\nenvironment variable substitution: {env.HCC_ENV_URL}\n\nThis caused Chrome shell routes to fail because Caddy couldn''t resolve\nthe stage environment URL.\n\n## Solution\n- Changed template to use correct Caddy syntax: ${HCC_ENV_URL}\n- Updated all test expectations to use correct syntax\n- Added validation checks in 7 tests to prevent regression\n\n## Changes\n- template/proxy_caddy.template.j2: Fixed env var syntax\n- tests/*: Updated assertions and added negative validation\n- CLAUDE.md: Added comprehensive documentation about:\n  - Correct vs incorrect Caddy syntax\n  - New \"Common Issue\" entry for this problem\n  - CRITICAL warnings to prevent future regressions\n\n## Test Coverage\nAll proxy generation tests now verify that {env.HCC_ENV_URL} does NOT\nappear in generated configs, ensuring the correct ${HCC_ENV_URL} syntax\nis always used.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: use direct URL substitution and remove routing directives from app ConfigMap\n\n## Changes\n\n### Direct URL Substitution\n- Added --stage-env-url CLI argument (required when Chrome routes exist)\n- Template now uses direct substitution: {{ stage_env_url }} instead of ${HCC_ENV_URL}\n- Eliminates Caddy environment variable resolution issues\n- Validation fails with clear error if stage_env_url not provided\n\n### Removed Routing Directives from App ConfigMap\n- Removed all try_files and rewrite directives from app template\n- App container only serves static files (fed-mods.json, JS bundles)\n- Proxy handles all routing logic\n- App ConfigMap now only contains asset routes (/apps/*, /settings/*)\n\n### Updated Validation\n- Renamed validate_federated_module_config → validate_app_config\n- Now validates NO app configs contain try_files or rewrite\n- Added tests for both try_files and rewrite rejection\n\n### Test Coverage\n- Updated all 29 tests to provide stage_env_url values\n- Added validation tests to prevent routing directives in app configs\n- Tests verify no ${HCC_ENV_URL} or {env.HCC_ENV_URL} in generated files\n\n## Breaking Change\n--stage-env-url is now REQUIRED when generating proxy ConfigMaps with Chrome routes\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove leading/trailing whitespace from generated ConfigMaps\n\n## Problem\nGenerated ConfigMaps had extra blank lines at the start of the data\nsection, causing yamllint to fail when committing the files.\n\n## Solution\n- Added .strip() to clean template output before indenting\n- Fixed Jinja2 template to use {%- and -%} for whitespace control\n- Removed leading/trailing newlines from rendered content\n\n## Result\nGenerated ConfigMaps now pass yamllint validation without extra\nblank lines at the start of data sections.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: remove catch-all root handler from app ConfigMap\n\n## Problem\nThe app ConfigMap template had a catch-all `handle /` directive that would\nredirect to /apps/chrome/index.html. This was problematic because:\n\n1. The app container on port 8000 should never receive requests to /\n2. The proxy routes /* to the stage environment, not localhost:8000\n3. This catch-all could interfere with routing if proxy logic changes\n4. It''s unnecessary - app container only serves its asset routes\n\n## Solution\nRemoved the `handle /` block entirely from app_caddy.template.j2\n\n## Result\nApp ConfigMap now only contains handlers for its specific asset routes:\n- /apps/rbac\n- /settings/rbac\n\nNo catch-all routes that could interfere with proxy routing.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: update CLAUDE.md to reflect proxy architecture changes\n\nUpdate documentation to reflect the new architecture where app ConfigMap\nonly serves static assets and proxy ConfigMap handles all routing logic.\nDocument direct URL substitution approach via --stage-env-url argument.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpj6y6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUk4QAJ/qOmUZzgEl/3wZ2iMbSk4H\nFJslHlOXU2sz+seeQJzBZu4fJ+gdrcG40puQf+xJAZoUXlTJ34WbEg57ntmMNaSA\nX+EtB7U/mAnxWFAils4Nuzoi2CvkYZtfPLKAiGdyqwGnzxCAKHoGwQJvCI5BoFj1\npYIFFTR4yG2HfV+SinFz80A0ijtP4WgVkT44DyY33jBf9jTztyJzYJi8VVxvdXc9\nhu3IjoL211mfLjUWR2dHSpf1qwBld9OyKh/0zwWS56B9yww0X1Q/+TNYc9+jop4F\n5AnOezBYp1XBuKly2rId5obcZYLr59d/GlcRMgCLx6LaqPV6LnOUo0j3++3y2tAr\nou+ro5QZMftVPAmOQ7bK2a8+A37+RlXeYq+ksGFiKsNZ22NFyfavZi57dKIQAllk\n+BFxvXjpRoeQF+4UmSnWwMBm0nyd5o+oTHSCo+/ZDYIgJkwwHyotMsGMaNreuT6C\nBPQV7CJ7TpJjixy0OqRDBUiwGgoGmwifj8sjdMjbF097ZDQL8ttkRezboCLhRoTL\nn2NX1lQA0YfSw47GptWHRNu320tUL2SQEpi/oPxwvhyAxPJ62vmlNP4ZMM7jTV86\nZmMS5c3kjdEBVtBrGEtWcEWkEsOkBayyeEHfLIF/iFM/yH3flvPknxoHztwmB2kV\n3nuGlCtoC8w7jMYYBC1b\n=ZA3l\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-13T22:59:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","follo