","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon","id":20647751,"login":"catastrophe-brandon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQ3NzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/3559a33eae675dbdea0117c3274d1a679921ea45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-12T23:07:04Z","email":"btweed@redhat.com","name":"Brandon Tweed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-12T23:07:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: proxy ConfigMap should only route asset paths, not navigation routes (#11)\n\n## Problem\nThe proxy ConfigMap was routing ALL paths (including navigation routes like\n/iam/my-user-access) to port 8000 (the local app container). This caused empty\nHTML pages because:\n1. Browser requests /iam/my-user-access (a navigation route)\n2. Proxy sends it to port 8000 (app container serving static assets)\n3. Port 8000 has no HTML for navigation routes, returns empty page\n\nNavigation routes should be handled by the Chrome shell in the stage\nenvironment, not the local app container.\n\n## Solution\nCreated distinction between:\n\n**Proxy routes (asset paths)** - Should route to port 8000:\n- spec.frontend.paths[] (e.g., /apps/rbac)\n- spec.module.modules[].routes[] (e.g., /settings/rbac, /iam)\n\n**Navigation routes** - Should fall through to Chrome shell:\n- spec.searchEntries[].href (e.g., /iam/user-access/users)\n- spec.serviceTiles[].href (e.g., /iam/user-access/groups)\n- spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[] (e.g., /iam/my-user-access)\n\n## Changes\n- Added get_proxy_routes_from_frontend_yaml() to extract only asset paths\n- Updated main.py to use proxy routes for proxy ConfigMap generation\n- Updated test to verify navigation routes are excluded from proxy config\n- Updated CLAUDE.md with detailed explanation of the distinction\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bbeaeb42216d6a0bcf238b00261878a754ce8c0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/trees/bbeaeb42216d6a0bcf238b00261878a754ce8c0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/commits/3559a33eae675dbdea0117c3274d1a679921ea45","verification":{"payload":"tree bbeaeb42216d6a0bcf238b00261878a754ce8c0a\nparent 67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1770937624 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770937624 -0600\n\nfix: proxy ConfigMap should only route asset paths, not navigation routes (#11)\n\n## Problem\nThe proxy ConfigMap was routing ALL paths (including navigation routes like\n/iam/my-user-access) to port 8000 (the local app container). This caused empty\nHTML pages because:\n1. Browser requests /iam/my-user-access (a navigation route)\n2. Proxy sends it to port 8000 (app container serving static assets)\n3. Port 8000 has no HTML for navigation routes, returns empty page\n\nNavigation routes should be handled by the Chrome shell in the stage\nenvironment, not the local app container.\n\n## Solution\nCreated distinction between:\n\n**Proxy routes (asset paths)** - Should route to port 8000:\n- spec.frontend.paths[] (e.g., /apps/rbac)\n- spec.module.modules[].routes[] (e.g., /settings/rbac, /iam)\n\n**Navigation routes** - Should fall through to Chrome shell:\n- spec.searchEntries[].href (e.g., /iam/user-access/users)\n- spec.serviceTiles[].href (e.g., /iam/user-access/groups)\n- spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[] (e.g., /iam/my-user-access)\n\n## Changes\n- Added get_proxy_routes_from_frontend_yaml() to extract only asset paths\n- Updated main.py to use proxy routes for proxy ConfigMap generation\n- Updated test to verify navigation routes are excluded from proxy config\n- Updated CLAUDE.md with detailed explanation of the distinction\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpjl0YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwBYQAJikVx+Z50Bn5YDWf//zNRqs\nbgiXbiMIuoSncIXR+zgiEDBCnndf5T++7aNeDi6Gfeq5tVoduDmC09oGweBsKhJi\nO2gA95tMhkGsUa/nl+QKSuKbv6SQWk3Q1zvarwQN+mIg0mT8PxTCzd6fwhGjCM4s\nLx8jj7n2RI5tHNlAq4fTrMVWs0urBilT0qQDDZMIfWEhmECeOsJ9Z9voawNhv7+i\nogPMMCbVTOVrVIi7OTyQ077S2rlJpco0k4qXQoW3sNN94b1WQf51bEJ9Kl1J1DFe\n4wVrHtKqR2zQqC/KNLYT23/dCGZaN8gz77D7ZgVt93h6d2wAeK/w11VKf4ZUEBPA\n3Ed+JNW6ir8xXN4WkE3h25mI+IHTexJOm9bWswIHTe5Aq9X/sSvCM4uI4D+gQN5h\nfLKy1mJdbgNoOtfkeJnP5PPEkDOm9FTJTDTQNOSY3wMl+PoSA/dcRCm5LBuPHRNi\n7WZRc+E8oFeCFW8KZO7ds11pj1jZkCcsWbiDOILwEVQIpCJjH1tzbtSHQ2INHndm\ngb0i3Ribi4CPl97IKQVXwwCX/E7DVOtGmzZeX76OLo8NMsDmpwvvISov5aChg/qG\nMW8Q8bGmf+NjYHS5x8bQC8jUS6KAtWuR53mFW7PY/SaWpce/5K/JdjuVvuq9d0Ed\nSYqKShtzapXF4Zbi519f\n=N2+x\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-12T23:07:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commit/3559a33eae675dbdea0117c3274d1a679921ea45","node_id":"C_kwDOQgdkkdoAKDM1NTlhMzNlYWU2NzVkYmRlYTAxMTdjMzI3NGQxYTY3OTkyMWVhNDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commit/67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed","sha":"67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed"}],"sha":"3559a33eae675dbdea0117c3274d1a679921ea45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/3559a33eae675dbdea0117c3274d1a679921ea45"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20647751?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon","id":20647751,"login":"catastrophe-brandon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQ3NzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-11T23:59:54Z","email":"btweed@redhat.com","name":"Brandon Tweed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-11T23:59:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Misc fixes (#10)\n\n* feat: detect federated modules and auto-extract module names\n\nThis commit adds three major improvements to Plumber:\n\n1. **Federated Module Detection**\n   - Add is_federated_module() to detect federated modules by checking\n     for spec.module.manifestLocation in frontend.yaml\n   - Pass is_federated flag to Jinja2 template\n   - Conditionally omit try_files directives for federated modules\n   - Federated modules only serve fed-mods.json and JS bundles, not index.html\n   - This fixes empty HTML page issues in E2E tests\n\n2. **Auto-Extract Module Name from frontend.yaml**\n   - Add get_module_name_from_frontend_yaml() to extract metadata.name\n   - Override CLI app_name argument with extracted module name\n   - Prevents mismatches when repo name differs from module name\n   - Example: insights-rbac-ui (repo) vs rbac (module)\n\n3. **Remove Redundant Hardcoded Route**\n   - Remove hardcoded /apps/{{ app_name }}* route from template\n   - Dynamic routes from spec.frontend.paths already cover it\n   - Eliminates duplication and reduces config size\n\n4. **Add Documentation for Future Claude Instances**\n   - Create CLAUDE.md explaining federated module vs standalone app behavior\n   - Document why try_files is conditional\n   - Explain module name extraction and common issues\n   - Provide testing instructions and file structure overview\n\nThese changes ensure Plumber correctly handles both federated modules\nand standalone apps, generating appropriate Caddy configurations for each.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: remove nonsensical hardcoded app_name routes\n\nRemove the @{{ app_name }}_match and @{{ app_name }}_subpath route\npatterns from the template. These generated confusing routes like:\n- /rbac/rbac/ (doubled path that never gets used)\n- /rbac/* (bare module name without /apps or other prefix)\n\nThese hardcoded patterns don''t match any actual routes used by\nPlatform UI applications. All real routes come from spec.frontend.paths\nand spec.module.modules[].routes in frontend.yaml, which are already\nhandled by the dynamic route generation.\n\nThis cleanup makes generated Caddy configs clearer and easier to understand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add validation to ensure federated modules have no try_files directives\n\nAdd automatic validation that prevents federated module configurations from\ncontaining try_files directives, which would cause errors since federated\nmodules don''t have index.html files.\n\nChanges:\n- Add validate_federated_module_config() function to check for try_files\n- Integrate validation into generate_app_caddyfile() flow\n- Add 6 comprehensive tests covering validation scenarios\n- Update CLAUDE.md with validation documentation\n\nThe validation runs automatically during config generation and provides\nclear error messages if a federated module config incorrectly includes\ntry_files directives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9e80661a6492d26910813d7c3b9538df3b4014a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/trees/9e80661a6492d26910813d7c3b9538df3b4014a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/commits/67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed","verification":{"payload":"tree 9e80661a6492d26910813d7c3b9538df3b4014a6\nparent ae2e9cb1c9362285e34b623f26a389c6a2ae1288\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1770854394 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770854394 -0600\n\nMisc fixes (#10)\n\n* feat: detect federated modules and auto-extract module names\n\nThis commit adds three major improvements to Plumber:\n\n1. **Federated Module Detection**\n   - Add is_federated_module() to detect federated modules by checking\n     for spec.module.manifestLocation in frontend.yaml\n   - Pass is_federated flag to Jinja2 template\n   - Conditionally omit try_files directives for federated modules\n   - Federated modules only serve fed-mods.json and JS bundles, not index.html\n   - This fixes empty HTML page issues in E2E tests\n\n2. **Auto-Extract Module Name from frontend.yaml**\n   - Add get_module_name_from_frontend_yaml() to extract metadata.name\n   - Override CLI app_name argument with extracted module name\n   - Prevents mismatches when repo name differs from module name\n   - Example: insights-rbac-ui (repo) vs rbac (module)\n\n3. **Remove Redundant Hardcoded Route**\n   - Remove hardcoded /apps/{{ app_name }}* route from template\n   - Dynamic routes from spec.frontend.paths already cover it\n   - Eliminates duplication and reduces config size\n\n4. **Add Documentation for Future Claude Instances**\n   - Create CLAUDE.md explaining federated module vs standalone app behavior\n   - Document why try_files is conditional\n   - Explain module name extraction and common issues\n   - Provide testing instructions and file structure overview\n\nThese changes ensure Plumber correctly handles both federated modules\nand standalone apps, generating appropriate Caddy configurations for each.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: remove nonsensical hardcoded app_name routes\n\nRemove the @{{ app_name }}_match and @{{ app_name }}_subpath route\npatterns from the template. These generated confusing routes like:\n- /rbac/rbac/ (doubled path that never gets used)\n- /rbac/* (bare module name without /apps or other prefix)\n\nThese hardcoded patterns don''t match any actual routes used by\nPlatform UI applications. All real routes come from spec.frontend.paths\nand spec.module.modules[].routes in frontend.yaml, which are already\nhandled by the dynamic route generation.\n\nThis cleanup makes generated Caddy configs clearer and easier to understand.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add validation to ensure federated modules have no try_files directives\n\nAdd automatic validation that prevents federated module configurations from\ncontaining try_files directives, which would cause errors since federated\nmodules don''t have index.html files.\n\nChanges:\n- Add validate_federated_module_config() function to check for try_files\n- Integrate validation into generate_app_caddyfile() flow\n- Add 6 comprehensive tests covering validation scenarios\n- Update CLAUDE.md with validation documentation\n\nThe validation runs automatically during config generation and provides\nclear error messages if a federated module config incorrectly includes\ntry_files directives.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpjRf6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvmQQAKTveqy9oM45vZLfwCu+ebeI\nfqRmPllYaGnM9DTncZW8hF/XaDs1Lvu3xbxF8KSouEpitechOuzxJiyKM0MG8SB0\nKh6JH9bYjWZJCYMrQH9OWHTybxoSUit2q6jw6XAwomUv+/1UJYCQOct4NykwWCzq\n85aKIprHOnR66SBH4YPUsuNeer06qofiJYHLuEzYii2OuLEFYlfx7zPxIZsMKar1\n0KuoyuPj3PO63VdTzGVEv+6B56xNEDym4EMWvxznhSqgPhCNyZI38iTBbjG17uCk\nmIJORTti+Qs5+CDZj1vY4m6s/acZOwFbdQXjuEPfMhRfY0u3rsdC89eG2fg4yKqy\nZSaCpDEwV3TOx8c76eZ6ZXM1CaUo8XN+tN0KbuGmZPtkrXuS6lwupyESiLnwKmqr\n+uUJqUNU/Vy+b5/YVpMWHcB1++T9cqo0wowWrDHrlCNwV28hlBMDZhqkV56AJyCx\nkoNU7egXA+LFWw/B0MpN0S5TUtqtqiPL6lcjMHz/zrHoFrEFP3jjNvfiyTKcPGd9\njCvgDqtIbXPjl0v5e/7zmtl1kHWDPrgXtw7sbSoOyVslIEieohoXtCbfAAb7rLds\nHEgKqNR2KWxR2gEhAl2Cs7qKaIau41kI+4qOCxLYPY+jzNll55fQiv88v+2pl58D\nXM0cmB9OCFG+3H6d9lNL\n=ETO6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-02-11T23:59:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commit/67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed","node_id":"C_kwDOQgdkkdoAKDY3ZWQwMTVmNjg4ODliYjYwMzUyNzEwNGNjOGFhMmUxNWFiYmVhZWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commit/ae2e9cb1c9362285e34b623f26a389c6a2ae1288","sha":"ae2e9cb1c9362285e34b623f26a389c6a2ae1288","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/ae2e9cb1c9362285e34b623f26a389c6a2ae1288"}],"sha":"67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/67ed015f68889bb603527104cc8aa2e15abbeaed"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20647751?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/catastrophe-brandon","id":20647751,"login":"catastrophe-brandon","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNjQ3NzUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/catastrophe-brandon","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/commits/ae2e9cb1c9362285e34b623f26a389c6a2ae1288/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-09T20:25:33Z","email":"btweed@redhat.com","name":"Brandon Tweed"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-09T20:25:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Update path generation logic/templates (#9)\n\n* Updates to incorporate pulling application paths from frontend.yaml when present\n\n* Add navigation route extraction and client-side routing support\n\nEnhanced plumber to extract all navigation routes from frontend.yaml\nand added proper client-side routing support for SPAs.\n\nFrontend YAML extraction improvements:\n- Extract routes from spec.searchEntries[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.serviceTiles[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].routes[].href\n- Added _extract_nav_item_hrefs() helper function for recursive extraction\n\nThis enables extraction of nested navigation routes like:\n- /iam/user-access/users\n- /iam/user-access/groups\n- /iam/access-management/users-and-user-groups\n- /iam/organization-management/authentication-factors\n- And many more from the navigation structure\n\nClient-side routing support:\n- Added try_files directive to app Caddy template\n- Serves index.html as fallback for non-existent files\n- Enables proper SPA routing for React Router and similar\n- Applied to all route handlers (app route, env route, dynamic routes)\n\nTesting:\n- Added test_frontend_yaml_extracts_navigation_routes()\n- Verifies all navigation route types are extracted\n- Verifies routes make it into generated Caddy ConfigMaps\n- All 23 tests pass\n\nDocumentation:\n- Updated README with enhanced extraction capabilities\n- Documented all new navigation route sources\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add federated module detection and skip index.html fallback\n\nFederated modules don''t have index.html files - they''re loaded dynamically\nby Chrome. This update detects federated modules and removes the try_files\nfallback to index.html in the generated Caddyfile.\n\nDetection:\n- Check for spec.module.manifestLocation in frontend.yaml\n- If present, app is a federated module\n\nChanges:\n- Add is_federated_module() function to extraction/__init__.py\n- Pass is_federated_module parameter through generation chain\n- Update app_caddy.template.j2 with conditional try_files directives\n- Only include try_files for standalone SPAs, not federated modules\n\nTesting:\n- Tested with insights-rbac-ui (federated module)\n- Correctly detects manifestLocation and skips index.html fallback\n- Generated Caddyfile serves static assets without SPA routing\n\nFixes: Empty page responses for federated modules in E2E tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: fix proxy routing for federated modules\n\nFederated modules should have all routing handled by Chrome shell,\nwith only the /apps/[appname]/* route going to the app port for\nserving federated module assets.\n\nChanges:\n- Updated proxy_caddy.template.j2 with conditional routing logic\n- For federated modules:\n  - /apps/[appname]/* → app_port (assets only)\n  - All other routes → chrome_port (HTML and routing)\n- For standalone apps: All routes → app_port (existing behavior)\n- Pass is_federated_module through proxy generation chain\n\nExample routing for RBAC UI (federated module):\n- /apps/rbac/* → 8000 (federated module JS/CSS/JSON)\n- /iam/* → 9912 (Chrome shell serves HTML)\n- /settings/rbac/* → 9912 (Chrome shell serves HTML)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove Chrome container dependency and simplify routing\n\nSimplified plumber by removing the insights-chrome-dev container\ndependency. All apps now serve routes directly without a Chrome shell.\n\nTemplate changes:\n- Removed chrome_port parameter from all functions\n- Removed is_federated_module parameter (no longer needed)\n- Simplified proxy template to only route to app port\n- Removed root, index.html, and /apps/chrome* handlers\n- All routes now go directly to the app container\n\nRoute extraction enhancements:\n- Extract routes from spec.searchEntries[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.serviceTiles[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].routes[].href\n\nClient-side routing support:\n- Added try_files directive to app Caddy template\n- Serves index.html as fallback for non-existent files\n- Enables proper SPA routing for React Router\n\nTesting:\n- Updated all tests to remove chrome_port references\n- Added test for navigation route extraction\n- All 23 tests pass\n\nThis simplifies the dev environment by removing the need for a separate\nChrome shell container and federated module complexity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a1179c0c774b284084b71b50c8e23f642107a39","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/trees/1a1179c0c774b284084b71b50c8e23f642107a39"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/commits/ae2e9cb1c9362285e34b623f26a389c6a2ae1288","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a1179c0c774b284084b71b50c8e23f642107a39\nparent 27b6a0539c06ef18d7e70b8b51fba9fc512b5142\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1770668733 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1770668733 -0600\n\nUpdate path generation logic/templates (#9)\n\n* Updates to incorporate pulling application paths from frontend.yaml when present\n\n* Add navigation route extraction and client-side routing support\n\nEnhanced plumber to extract all navigation routes from frontend.yaml\nand added proper client-side routing support for SPAs.\n\nFrontend YAML extraction improvements:\n- Extract routes from spec.searchEntries[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.serviceTiles[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].routes[].href\n- Added _extract_nav_item_hrefs() helper function for recursive extraction\n\nThis enables extraction of nested navigation routes like:\n- /iam/user-access/users\n- /iam/user-access/groups\n- /iam/access-management/users-and-user-groups\n- /iam/organization-management/authentication-factors\n- And many more from the navigation structure\n\nClient-side routing support:\n- Added try_files directive to app Caddy template\n- Serves index.html as fallback for non-existent files\n- Enables proper SPA routing for React Router and similar\n- Applied to all route handlers (app route, env route, dynamic routes)\n\nTesting:\n- Added test_frontend_yaml_extracts_navigation_routes()\n- Verifies all navigation route types are extracted\n- Verifies routes make it into generated Caddy ConfigMaps\n- All 23 tests pass\n\nDocumentation:\n- Updated README with enhanced extraction capabilities\n- Documented all new navigation route sources\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: add federated module detection and skip index.html fallback\n\nFederated modules don''t have index.html files - they''re loaded dynamically\nby Chrome. This update detects federated modules and removes the try_files\nfallback to index.html in the generated Caddyfile.\n\nDetection:\n- Check for spec.module.manifestLocation in frontend.yaml\n- If present, app is a federated module\n\nChanges:\n- Add is_federated_module() function to extraction/__init__.py\n- Pass is_federated_module parameter through generation chain\n- Update app_caddy.template.j2 with conditional try_files directives\n- Only include try_files for standalone SPAs, not federated modules\n\nTesting:\n- Tested with insights-rbac-ui (federated module)\n- Correctly detects manifestLocation and skips index.html fallback\n- Generated Caddyfile serves static assets without SPA routing\n\nFixes: Empty page responses for federated modules in E2E tests\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: fix proxy routing for federated modules\n\nFederated modules should have all routing handled by Chrome shell,\nwith only the /apps/[appname]/* route going to the app port for\nserving federated module assets.\n\nChanges:\n- Updated proxy_caddy.template.j2 with conditional routing logic\n- For federated modules:\n  - /apps/[appname]/* → app_port (assets only)\n  - All other routes → chrome_port (HTML and routing)\n- For standalone apps: All routes → app_port (existing behavior)\n- Pass is_federated_module through proxy generation chain\n\nExample routing for RBAC UI (federated module):\n- /apps/rbac/* → 8000 (federated module JS/CSS/JSON)\n- /iam/* → 9912 (Chrome shell serves HTML)\n- /settings/rbac/* → 9912 (Chrome shell serves HTML)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove Chrome container dependency and simplify routing\n\nSimplified plumber by removing the insights-chrome-dev container\ndependency. All apps now serve routes directly without a Chrome shell.\n\nTemplate changes:\n- Removed chrome_port parameter from all functions\n- Removed is_federated_module parameter (no longer needed)\n- Simplified proxy template to only route to app port\n- Removed root, index.html, and /apps/chrome* handlers\n- All routes now go directly to the app container\n\nRoute extraction enhancements:\n- Extract routes from spec.searchEntries[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.serviceTiles[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].href\n- Extract routes from spec.bundleSegments[].navItems[].routes[].href\n\nClient-side routing support:\n- Added try_files directive to app Caddy template\n- Serves index.html as fallback for non-existent files\n- Enables proper SPA routing for React Router\n\nTesting:\n- Updated all tests to remove chrome_port references\n- Added test for navigation route extraction\n- All 23 tests pass\n\nThis simplifies the dev environment by removing the need for a separate\nChrome shell container and federated module complexity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpikK9CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+yQQAJBeICUMhXAwZVtgmmk+xBB3\nlTcLlZTrLkjVdFm4GS7TqkbRBc7Ky+wqz13QxM9CuI+DXjpMBGcLY/lBvZeWqF7b\n+bPGcYDb6v46rqqv8Fq9pJxOlNErrHicZsuf8usvhwtZH7JuicbwOkJCs3sE2PGF\ncxCG3LOdIxpjGc+npYxwBJqp5uYdOmSQBZwtuTx+Zhii5OCmtIfRaLWDSb4/vBPM\nUxgiX/pJBiQWQ+jF3JgC+tPA7B9yp5cG3q/2ZU4PAP20DKDpeX/ekRa7oSQJNZuS\njxkpd0oJ9ojM72KrveG/iVn/UPk/ZwUnOL/WDrKZtrMi+Fj5k17Dkt1Kc5jznLlG\ndgmgtY2rk7YeUj8GmCYsNx+qPc4D2ggA7Itx1TAqw5rm0R43EPCvi+d/N16oWr8z\njXtkdgyLmKje9fcQt1OJnBUIH1mEfKW+W2Q359/tKI8xFbR3aSvlktYndymGbU5m\nXDyKW4qbYJ24ik8Cuu2XC/+8OMDEEETwYFnpbkNU8SFNZK