l tests use pytest''s tmp_path fixture for automatic cleanup, preventing test artifacts from polluting the working directory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove duplicate def\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"115110f9f29f8f3138352c46e1318666e5429ac0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/trees/115110f9f29f8f3138352c46e1318666e5429ac0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/commits/27b6a0539c06ef18d7e70b8b51fba9fc512b5142","verification":{"payload":"tree 115110f9f29f8f3138352c46e1318666e5429ac0\nparent 11e61f1852c32d749b5b7fc95b5860e09d5faada\nauthor Brandon Tweed <btweed@redhat.com> 1768951404 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1768951404 -0600\n\nAdd tests to confirm fallback behavior when frontend.yaml isn''t found (#8)\n\n* Updates to incorporate pulling application paths from frontend.yaml when present\n\n* Fix formatting issues and add a script to install a git hook\n\n* Add comprehensive tests for frontend.yaml to fec.config.js fallback behavior\n\nAdded three new tests to verify the complete fallback chain:\n- test_fallback_from_frontend_yaml_to_fec_config: Tests fallback to fec.config.js when frontend.yaml is missing\n- test_fallback_to_default_when_both_missing: Tests fallback to default routes when both files are missing\n- test_frontend_yaml_takes_precedence_over_fec_config: Tests that frontend.yaml takes precedence when both files exist\n\nAll tests use pytest''s tmp_path fixture for automatic cleanup, preventing test artifacts from polluting the working directory.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Remove duplicate def\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpcA5sCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAovEQAK0S6+YJ/C6+oM9x5FUxCdny\nsyWvskNoS1xySUMSUeu6ROmpxP8BHV9rO03hp5W6Unp