l 20 tests passing\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Update README with comprehensive documentation\n\n- Added detailed overview of Plumber''s functionality\n- Updated CLI usage section with new command syntax\n- Added example output showing what users can expect\n- Documented all new features:\n  - App Caddyfile generation\n  - Proxy Caddyfile generation\n  - JavaScript config parsing\n  - YAML validation\n- Updated Python API examples\n- Added \"How It Works\" section\n- Updated project structure with all test files\n- Added comprehensive test coverage documentation\n- Listed all requirements including pyyaml\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Use recently merged pipeline definition in konflux-pipelines in template\n\n* Update pipeline reference to use Caddyfile-accepting version\n\n- Changed revision from ''main'' to commit c956d1b09d2d6bb70110f7e6f67029276eb9f62a\n- This commit includes pipeline changes to accept Caddyfile format\n  for proxy-routes-script instead of JSON\n- Pipeline now executes the script and saves output directly to\n  /config/Caddyfile for the frontend-dev-proxy sidecar\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix pipeline URL to point to fork instead of upstream\n\n- Changed URL from RedHatInsights/konflux-pipelines to catastrophe-brandon/konflux-pipelines\n- This ensures the pipeline uses the fork with Caddyfile-accepting changes\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Switch to JSON format for proxy routes to work with standard pipeline\n\n- Added generate_proxy_routes_json() function to create JSON route config\n- Updated template to output JSON directly instead of shell script\n- Updated template to point to RedHatInsights/konflux-pipelines main\n- Updated run_plumber() to use JSON generator for proxy routes\n- App Caddyfile generation remains unchanged\n\nThis allows using the standard Konflux pipeline without modifications\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Fix YAML validation error with compact JSON format\n\n- Changed JSON generation to use compact single-line format\n- This prevents YAML parser from misinterpreting JSON as YAML structure\n- Updated template to use |- (literal style, strip trailing newlines)\n- YAML now validates successfully\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Wrap JSON in bash script for proxy-routes-script parameter\n\n- Changed template to wrap JSON in a bash script with heredoc\n- The pipeline executes this script and writes output to /config/routes\n- Removed indentation for JSON since it''s inside a heredoc\n- Script outputs compact single-line JSON\n- Validated: script executes successfully and produces valid JSON\n\nThis matches the expected format for the standard Konflux pipeline\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Refactoring, support for new type of pipeline generation. Generate Caddyfile config instead of JSON\n\n* Formatting\n\n* Ruff appeasement\n\n* Update proj deps\n\n* Generate the application sidecar''s caddy configuration\n\n* Update docs\n\n* Use a different version of the shared pipeline def\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0909f1308b1c41068fc1dab34ae3ce8ecdcf87fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/trees/0909f1308b1c41068fc1dab34ae3ce8ecdcf87fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/catastrophe-brandon/plumber/git/commits/cf430b9e73a9bc73a96a4924d1401e88d0cd0c2c","verification":{"payload":"tree 090